      "sentences": [
        {
          "sid": "drinks-t1-s01",
          "c": "我想飲杯咖啡。",
          "j": "ngo5 soeng2 jam2 bui1 gaa3 fe1.",
          "e": "I want to drink a coffee.",
          "note": "In casual speech the 一 (jat1) \"one\" before a classifier often drops — 飲杯咖啡 (jam2 bui1 gaa3 fe1) \"drink a coffee\", short for 飲一杯咖啡 (jam2 jat1 bui1 gaa3 fe1). 杯 (bui1) \"cup\" is the classifier for drinks.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "想",
              "j": "soeng2",
              "e": "want to"
            },
            {
              "c": "飲",
              "j": "jam2",
              "e": "drink"
            },
            {
              "c": "杯",
              "j": "bui1",
              "e": "a cup of"
            },
            {
              "c": "咖啡",
              "j": "gaa3 fe1",
              "e": "coffee"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "drinks-t1-s02",
          "c": "凍檸茶唔該！",
          "j": "dung3 ning4 caa4 m4 goi1!",
          "e": "Iced lemon tea, please!",
          "note": "凍 (dung3) means \"cold / iced\" (opposite 熱 jit6 \"hot\") — 凍檸茶 (dung3 ning4 caa4) \"iced lemon tea\", a cha chaan teng classic. 檸 (ning4) is short for 檸檬 (ning4 mung1) \"lemon\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "凍檸茶",
              "j": "dung3 ning4 caa4",
              "e": "iced lemon tea"
            },
            {
              "c": "唔該",
              "j": "m4 goi1",
              "e": "please"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "drinks-t1-s03",
          "c": "你想飲茶定咖啡？",
          "j": "nei5 soeng2 jam2 caa4 ding6 gaa3 fe1?",
          "e": "Do you want tea or coffee?",
          "note": "定 (ding6) \"or\" offers a choice between two options — 茶定咖啡？(caa4 ding6 gaa3 fe1?) \"tea or coffee?\". (Not the same as listing with 同 tung4 \"and\".)",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "你",
              "j": "nei5",
              "e": "you"
            },
            {
              "c": "想飲",
              "j": "soeng2 jam2",
              "e": "want to drink"
            },
            {
              "c": "茶",
              "j": "caa4",
              "e": "tea"
            },
            {
              "c": "定",
              "j": "ding6",
              "e": "or"
            },
            {
              "c": "咖啡",
              "j": "gaa3 fe1",
              "e": "coffee"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "drinks-t1-s04",
          "c": "細路唔可以飲啤酒。",
          "j": "sai3 lou6 m4 ho2 ji5 jam2 be1 zau2.",
          "e": "Children can't drink beer.",
          "note": "細路 (sai3 lou6) is the casual Cantonese for \"kid / child\". 唔可以 (m4 ho2 ji5) is \"may not / not allowed\". 啤酒 (be1 zau2) \"beer\" — 啤 (be1) is borrowed from English.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "細路",
              "j": "sai3 lou6",
              "e": "children"
